hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1647","Narrated to us by Bundar and Abu Musa, who said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Dhar, from the son of 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Abza, from his father, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, who said: \"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was leading the prayer, and he omitted a verse. Among the congregation was Ubayy ibn Ka'b, so he said"
"1648","###\n Muhammad bin Yahya narrated to us, and Muhammad bin Amr bin Tamim al-Misri narrated to us; they both said: Yusuf bin Adi narrated to us, who said: Marwan bin Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Yahya bin Kathir al-Kahili, from Miswar bin Yazid al-Usaydi. Muhammad bin Yahya (in his narration) said: \"I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)...\" while Muhammad bin Amr said: \"The Messenger of Allah ("
